      "writtenOn": "2026-07-22T09:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the feedback. We understand the architectural concern — `canHostTasks()` is derived from `MIRROR_BUILT_IN_DISPLAY`, so writing back to the setting based on a derived value is logically circular.\n\nHowever, to give context on why we added this: `ENABLE_DISPLAY_CONTENT_MODE_MANAGEMENT` was also enabled in Android 16, but simultaneous mirroring + activity launch on external displays worked fine there. In Android 17, looks like `forceEnableMirrorBuiltInDisplaySettingIfNeeded()` is now forcing `MIRROR_BUILT_IN_DISPLAY\u003d1`, which causes `canHostTasks()` to return false on all external displays, blocking activity routing.\n\nCould you help clarify the correct Android 17 mechanism for AAOS to support simultaneous mirroring and activity hosting on external displays? Specifically,should `forceEnableMirrorBuiltInDisplaySettingIfNeeded()` be gated for automotive, or is there a different path we should be using?",
